homeowners in oregon evacuation zones  are now worried about their belongings  being stolen while they're not home  our reporter kate houston is live  tonight outside the clackamas county  sheriff's office  which is about 11 miles southeast of  portland so  deputies have received many calls over  the past week  yeah that's right sasha the sheriff's  department says calls for service have  exploded in level two and level three  evacuation zones  many of these are reports for suspicious  people cars and  concerns about burglaries i spoke to a  family who says  that their home was looted after they  had to evacuate from estacada  this week the patterson family left  their home on tuesday  as evacuation levels were increasing on  friday morning they got a notification  from their alarm system  saying someone went inside their home  video of the aftermath shows  red bull cans thrown around the kitchen  dog food  everywhere and many items stolen chuck  patterson tells me over 60 necklaces  and 100 pairs of his wife's earrings are  missing  much of it was passed down by family  members some were from patterson himself  as they were dating in high school  he tells me his wife is devastated and  he's furious  we just want to get back to our home but  with the smoke there we can't get back  my son is actually at the house down  he's you know it's a level three  evacuation  and my son is risking his life to stay  in our house  to make it so idiots don't do this  patterson shared these videos and photos  taken from his doorbell camera  the family says they found knives around  the house and a bb gun sitting outside  as well  they're asking anyone with information  to contact the police  now the clackamas county sheriff's  office will be increasing patrols  in level two and level three evacuation  zones and this is to protect homes  and businesses reporting live from  clackamas oregon tonight kate houston 8  news now  so kate is the sheriff's office  receiving any help with the amount of  calls they're getting and of course the  magnitude of these evacuations  yes they are sasha the multnomah county  sheriff's office and  oregon state police are here to assist  them and they say  that from tuesday to thursday this week  they had 330 calls  for suspicious activity and that's more  than a 400 percent increase from the  days before  thank you so much and stay safe out  there sally
 

